{"event_type":"review","id":"d1e9e2c945ade75ad98a380cb96f7640198bbf32912fe3dad48f177bd129b2cf","occurred_at":"2026-11-06T05:44:50Z","payload":{"artifacts":[{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/659a382def0b3a34a93c7cad7cc4e243e09aabcc77a7de170f706ef767cfb4bf","sha256":"659a382def0b3a34a93c7cad7cc4e243e09aabcc77a7de170f706ef767cfb4bf"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/ecab6cb06f547bbf431a56ea90f8eab41c7c12a661150e962594a38100022d01","sha256":"ecab6cb06f547bbf431a56ea90f8eab41c7c12a661150e962594a38100022d01"},{"kind":"git-bundle","location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/008610d49d521d49da976a64704004b2a670104b9e4c88bfceb72d6997bfb64e","sha256":"008610d49d521d49da976a64704004b2a670104b9e4c88bfceb72d6997bfb64e"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/e38c11d3806fc545f98b3dbd5a1ba0baa14603ff385dfa87bf7fb416518d664f","sha256":"e38c11d3806fc545f98b3dbd5a1ba0baa14603ff385dfa87bf7fb416518d664f"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/b6630d5171f79b7d440952a2bb4c44221ae4d4f4365b88c5f61bc4a584976e81","sha256":"b6630d5171f79b7d440952a2bb4c44221ae4d4f4365b88c5f61bc4a584976e81"}],"attempt_id":"8f2e00db08dda1f3f415b4d6bf30f5bacae9ad5b44139e0f6c24105ecf2e0b1f:0:1","base":"f6be3614ab513781e65b18b3d6b54f4de3349ae7","completion":{"errors":[],"exit_code":0,"scope_verified":true,"skipped":false,"terminal":true},"findings":[{"anchor_status":"unverified","blob":"6fed7f0d0d15e85dd0b7f6b9ad6aceead30382e2","body":"**Keep `contextSha256` bound to the delivered prompt.**\n\nLines 404-410 replace `plan.prompt` with a repair prompt before each evidence-repair run. The `beforeRequest` hook then runs again. On a `contextOnly` session, Line 228 overwrites `evidence.contextSha256` with the hash of the repair prompt. Context-only sessions have no placements, so the `deliveries.length > 0` guard at Line 230 never stops this. The recorded hash then names the last repair prompt, not the context that was reviewed.\n\nA retry is unaffected: Line 334 deletes the hash before the second attempt, so the first-write guard still records the retried delivery.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🐛 Proposed fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n-      if (plan.contextOnly)\n+      if (plan.contextOnly && evidence.contextSha256 === undefined)\n         evidence.contextSha256 = createHash('sha256').update(plan.prompt).digest('hex');\n```\n</details>","id":"9b12dbbea8d470dce0e66a704f1d365ac3b6905d67b44388dd33846c9273e424","intervals":[],"path":"src/ops/review/internal/reviewSession.ts","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Keep `contextSha256` bound to the delivered prompt."},{"anchor_status":"unverified","blob":"d8e034c02e65dc3a1a98e262c434183cb9d3fccb","body":"**Remove settled sessions from `active` before the wall check.**\n\nIn `src/ops/review/agentReviewer.ts:390`, if a session finishes after the deadline and all workers settle before the timer fires, `ensureActive()` throws. The catch then changes the completed session’s status to `error`. Findings are retained through `onFindings`.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Suggested fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n         if (result.status !== 'ok' && result.status !== 'budget-exhausted') nonBudgetFailure = true;\n+        active.delete(evidence);\n         ensureActive();\n         updatePieces(report!.coverage);\n-        active.delete(evidence);\n```\n\n</details>","id":"3ba1139beefad6e92acd98e78f5b79aa619b7867db4248915bb18cbb22d37891","intervals":[],"path":"src/ops/review/agentReviewer.ts","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Remove settled sessions from `active` before the wall check."}],"head":"32e3d2309981792bfe832f17e515d7bd64aefd8a","head_tree":"013c2fa4bf520f2358e9d1367a3d73c21ab4fb44","input_scope":[{"blob":"d8e034c02e65dc3a1a98e262c434183cb9d3fccb","intervals":[[1,530]],"path":"src/ops/review/agentReviewer.ts"},{"blob":"d57d8ea3bb9c6e1e8d6d0a5af